From: Marmalade STT <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Cancel terminates the encoder run (#54)

Not upstream; ours, on top of 0003. 0003 stops a cancelled decode at its
next decoder step, but the encoder run before the first step couldn't be
stopped: a cancel during it waited 1.8 s on the host for 29.5 s of audio
(several seconds on a phone). OfflineStream now keeps the ONNX Runtime
RunOptions of the run in progress (CancellableRun, registered while it
lives) and Cancel() calls RunOptions::SetTerminate on them, so the run stops
between two graph nodes and throws. The encoder runs of Whisper and Canary
and Qwen3-ASR's conv frontend, encoder and prefill take these options; the
recognizers catch the exception of a cancelled stream and return no result.
Registering options on an already cancelled stream terminates them at once.
---
--- a/sherpa-onnx/csrc/offline-canary-model.cc
+++ b/sherpa-onnx/csrc/offline-canary-model.cc
@@ -66,12 +66,15 @@ class OfflineCanaryModel::Impl {
   }
 
   std::vector<Ort::Value> ForwardEncoder(Ort::Value features,
-                                         Ort::Value features_length) {
+                                         Ort::Value features_length,
+                                         const Ort::RunOptions *run_options) {
     std::array<Ort::Value, 2> encoder_inputs = {std::move(features),
                                                 std::move(features_length)};
 
+    Ort::RunOptions no_run_options{nullptr};
     auto encoder_out = encoder_sess_->Run(
-        {}, encoder_input_names_ptr_.data(), encoder_inputs.data(),
+        run_options ? *run_options : no_run_options,
+        encoder_input_names_ptr_.data(), encoder_inputs.data(),
         encoder_inputs.size(), encoder_output_names_ptr_.data(),
         encoder_output_names_ptr_.size());
 
@@ -244,8 +247,10 @@ OfflineCanaryModel::OfflineCanaryModel(Manager *mgr,
 OfflineCanaryModel::~OfflineCanaryModel() = default;
 
 std::vector<Ort::Value> OfflineCanaryModel::ForwardEncoder(
-    Ort::Value features, Ort::Value features_length) const {
-  return impl_->ForwardEncoder(std::move(features), std::move(features_length));
+    Ort::Value features, Ort::Value features_length,
+    const Ort::RunOptions *run_options) const {
+  return impl_->ForwardEncoder(std::move(features), std::move(features_length),
+                               run_options);
 }
 
